  "summary": "Malicious code in tcb-web-copy-to-clipboard (npm)",
  "details": "Tcb-web-copy-to-clipboard is a combosquat package impersonating a clipboard SDK. On require(), it fingerprints the host platform and architecture, then downloads a platform-specific binary payload from a set of Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to paths like /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS fails, it falls back to DNS-based payload retrieval via TXT record chunked queries to subdomains of dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom\u003e.exe on Windows) and executed as a detached background process.",
  "affected": [
    {
      "package": {
        "ecosystem": "npm",
        "name": "tcb-web-copy-to-clipboard",
        "purl": "pkg:npm/tcb-web-copy-to-clipboard"
